WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.349 --> 00:00:04.113 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson two.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:06.141 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What you are going to need.

00:00:06.952 --> 00:00:08.098 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.657 --> 00:00:09.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.491 --> 00:00:12.314 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information

00:00:12.314 --> 00:00:14.746 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.746 --> 00:00:16.646 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:18.930 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:23.192 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:23.192 --> 00:00:24.890 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.349 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the last

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:28.354 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price of that day.

00:00:28.855 --> 00:00:30.911 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:30.911 --> 00:00:32.673 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:33.873 --> 00:00:35.773 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:36.771 --> 00:00:39.279 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is a digital coin, such as bitcoin.

00:00:39.799 --> 00:00:41.933 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A range is the top and the bottom,

00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:44.314 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two lines,

00:00:44.314 --> 00:00:46.612 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the step is how wide that gap is.

00:00:47.132 --> 00:00:49.170 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.063 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
do if the price leaves the range.

00:00:51.583 --> 00:00:53.482 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Like a packing list before a trip,

00:00:53.482 --> 00:00:55.382 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your page comes before any screen.

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:57.814 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will fill in

00:00:57.814 --> 00:00:59.753 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a seven-item checklist on paper.

00:01:00.953 --> 00:01:03.244 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will keep every secret off that page.

00:01:04.251 --> 00:01:06.096 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will mark the page Example so

00:01:06.096 --> 00:01:07.828 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
nobody can read it as an order.

00:01:08.936 --> 00:01:11.100 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The seven items are: a notebook,

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.524 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
three words, range, levels and stop,

00:01:13.524 --> 00:01:15.775 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the pair, paper or a demo account,

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.852 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
no secrets, a written stop, and

00:01:17.852 --> 00:01:20.189 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the word Example on every figure.

00:01:20.709 --> 00:01:22.090 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each item has a reason.

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:23.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The notebook is the plan

00:01:23.951 --> 00:01:25.068 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can check later.

00:01:25.321 --> 00:01:26.662 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The three words stop you

00:01:26.662 --> 00:01:28.282 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
drawing a grid with no edges.

00:01:28.651 --> 00:01:29.936 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair names what you

00:01:29.936 --> 00:01:31.389 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy and what you pay with.

00:01:31.763 --> 00:01:33.227 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or a demo is learner

00:01:33.227 --> 00:01:34.761 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
plates, or training wheels.

00:01:35.281 --> 00:01:37.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No secrets keeps the keys off the page.

00:01:37.953 --> 00:01:39.684 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The written stop is the action.

00:01:39.977 --> 00:01:41.765 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example marks a teaching number.

00:01:42.176 --> 00:01:43.684 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the pair is

00:01:43.684 --> 00:01:45.323 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin priced in US dollars.

00:01:45.843 --> 00:01:48.035 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A demo account uses pretend money.

00:01:48.555 --> 00:01:49.974 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A daily close is the last

00:01:49.974 --> 00:01:50.924 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price of the day.

00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:52.869 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are naming that public

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:54.433 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
series, not choosing an app.

00:01:55.245 --> 00:01:56.977 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Three words, before any number.

00:01:57.382 --> 00:01:59.967 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:02.511 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy

00:02:02.511 --> 00:02:04.460 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
or sell that can wait for a price.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.347 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the price lines where orders

00:02:07.347 --> 00:02:09.414 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wait, like the rungs of a ladder, and

00:02:09.414 --> 00:02:11.593 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap is the space between two of them.

00:02:12.026 --> 00:02:14.374 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stop is the rule for what you will do if

00:02:14.374 --> 00:02:16.869 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a daily close finishes outside the range

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:19.364 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:02:19.884 --> 00:02:21.705 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The figures from lesson 1 are

00:02:21.705 --> 00:02:23.373 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on the card, marked Example.

00:02:23.893 --> 00:02:25.569 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If you can only say one of the

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:27.804 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
three words, the page is missing a part.

00:02:28.674 --> 00:02:30.797 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A wallet is where your crypto is held.

00:02:31.113 --> 00:02:33.013 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A seed phrase is the list of words

00:02:33.013 --> 00:02:34.420 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that unlocks that wallet.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.337 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A private key is a secret

00:02:36.337 --> 00:02:37.803 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can move your crypto.

00:02:38.323 --> 00:02:40.666 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An API secret is a password that lets

00:02:40.666 --> 00:02:43.008 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a program place orders on an account,

00:02:43.008 --> 00:02:45.194 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and sometimes move money out of it.

00:02:45.714 --> 00:02:48.341 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You never type a seed phrase, a private

00:02:48.341 --> 00:02:50.714 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret onto this page.

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:53.032 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart has no balance on it.

00:02:53.552 --> 00:02:55.508 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A public close is not your account.

00:02:55.983 --> 00:02:57.614 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a form asks for a secret,

00:02:57.614 --> 00:02:59.399 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that form is not this lesson.

00:03:00.449 --> 00:03:02.423 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You copy the range onto the page,

00:03:02.423 --> 00:03:03.865 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not every day's prices.

00:03:04.385 --> 00:03:06.619 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Copy the bottom line and the top

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.767 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, with six gaps of about 900.

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:10.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in that window

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.081 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed inside the range.

00:03:12.504 --> 00:03:13.907 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Mark each figure Example.

00:03:14.957 --> 00:03:16.573 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: pair, range,

00:03:16.573 --> 00:03:18.028 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gaps, stop, and Example.

00:03:18.548 --> 00:03:20.762 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the stop line is only a tick with no

00:03:20.762 --> 00:03:22.829 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sentence, the page fails the check.

00:03:23.349 --> 00:03:25.133 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rule has to say: if a daily

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:27.304 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close finishes outside the range

00:03:27.304 --> 00:03:29.398 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still

00:03:29.398 --> 00:03:31.182 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
outside, the example is over.

00:03:32.232 --> 00:03:34.243 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A page is the notebook you can hold.

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:36.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the app or website

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.662 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where people buy and sell crypto.

00:03:39.182 --> 00:03:40.690 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The screen is the exchange.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.643 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 1 ended by asking

00:03:42.643 --> 00:03:43.938 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you to bring the page.

00:03:44.458 --> 00:03:45.854 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson is that page.

00:03:46.369 --> 00:03:48.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Open the notebook before any screen.

00:03:49.291 --> 00:03:51.358 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write today's date on the first line.

00:03:51.707 --> 00:03:53.551 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Under it, write the word Example.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:55.413 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Example means a real past

00:03:55.413 --> 00:03:56.822 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price used for practice.

00:03:57.342 --> 00:03:59.464 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not an order and not a forecast.

00:04:00.589 --> 00:04:01.763 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the pair first.

00:04:02.166 --> 00:04:03.563 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The base is what you buy.

00:04:04.063 --> 00:04:05.795 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The quote is what you pay with.

00:04:06.129 --> 00:04:09.321 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For this course the prices are the July

00:04:09.321 --> 00:04:12.412 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window, the public

00:04:12.412 --> 00:04:15.105 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin closes from 19 July to 16

00:04:15.105 --> 00:04:17.698 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
October 2023, so you buy the base,

00:04:17.698 --> 00:04:20.490 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bitcoin, with the quote, US dollars,

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:23.183 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and that row is labelled BTC/USD.

00:04:23.703 --> 00:04:25.714 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every other row depends on the pair.

00:04:25.936 --> 00:04:27.517 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
We price in US dollars.

00:04:28.037 --> 00:04:29.789 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Your exchange may charge fees

00:04:29.789 --> 00:04:31.261 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars, so

00:04:31.261 --> 00:04:32.825 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
keep each in its own column.

00:04:33.323 --> 00:04:35.499 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a fee sum is in Australian

00:04:35.499 --> 00:04:37.675 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, that sum goes on its

00:04:37.675 --> 00:04:39.756 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
own line, labelled BTC/AUD.

00:04:40.276 --> 00:04:42.183 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Do not put a US dollar price and

00:04:42.183 --> 00:04:44.699 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
an Australian dollar fee on the same row.

00:04:45.749 --> 00:04:48.334 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

00:04:49.089 --> 00:04:53.571 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the July to October example window

00:04:54.068 --> 00:04:57.255 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
those lines are 24,930 and 30,331.

00:04:57.775 --> 00:04:59.171 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Both figures are Example.

00:04:59.675 --> 00:05:01.574 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Levels are the lines between them.

00:05:01.865 --> 00:05:04.023 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:05:04.023 --> 00:05:06.022 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the top and the bottom.

00:05:06.542 --> 00:05:08.397 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write the top and the bottom only

00:05:08.397 --> 00:05:10.409 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after you have said what a range is.

00:05:10.842 --> 00:05:12.732 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then write one gap, and how you

00:05:12.732 --> 00:05:14.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
got it: the top minus the bottom,

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:16.590 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by the number of gaps.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:18.911 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop sentence has

00:05:18.911 --> 00:05:20.252 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to say what you will do.

00:05:20.702 --> 00:05:22.509 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is a program that places

00:05:22.509 --> 00:05:24.919 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and cancels the waiting orders for you.

00:05:25.439 --> 00:05:27.561 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Two daily closes outside the range,

00:05:27.561 --> 00:05:29.317 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
through the top or the bottom,

00:05:29.317 --> 00:05:31.440 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the second close still outside.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.524 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then you stop the bot, which

00:05:33.524 --> 00:05:35.112 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cancels the waiting orders,

00:05:35.112 --> 00:05:37.011 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you follow the rule you wrote.

00:05:37.523 --> 00:05:39.311 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Write that stop in one sentence.

00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:43.003 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A deposit is crypto or Australian dollars

00:05:43.003 --> 00:05:45.500 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you send into an account at an exchange.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.036 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange in Australia asks who

00:05:48.036 --> 00:05:49.836 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you are before you can deposit.

00:05:50.356 --> 00:05:52.659 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That check is required by Australian

00:05:52.659 --> 00:05:54.590 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
anti-money laundering law, and

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:56.819 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the exchange runs it, not this course.

00:05:57.339 --> 00:05:59.343 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You only upload identification

00:05:59.343 --> 00:06:01.198 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
inside the exchange's own app.

00:06:01.718 --> 00:06:03.785 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name an exchange

00:06:03.785 --> 00:06:05.349 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and does not show a balance.

00:06:05.609 --> 00:06:08.152 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Any exchange offering crypto services

00:06:08.152 --> 00:06:10.771 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australia must register with AUSTRAC,

00:06:10.771 --> 00:06:13.390 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australia's financial crime regulator,

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.701 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as a virtual asset service provider.

00:06:16.221 --> 00:06:17.486 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
AUSTRAC keeps a public

00:06:17.486 --> 00:06:18.827 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
register you can search.

00:06:19.337 --> 00:06:21.516 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check that register before you sign up.

00:06:21.989 --> 00:06:24.280 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The register says the business is listed.

00:06:24.706 --> 00:06:26.941 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not say your money is protected.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.816 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Registration is not a safety guarantee.

00:06:30.336 --> 00:06:32.218 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC is Australia's financial

00:06:32.218 --> 00:06:33.448 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
services regulator.

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:36.872 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From April 2027, platforms that hold

00:06:36.872 --> 00:06:39.679 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto for you need an ASIC licence,

00:06:39.679 --> 00:06:42.583 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a transition period to October

00:06:42.583 --> 00:06:45.681 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2027 for platforms already operating.

00:06:46.201 --> 00:06:48.212 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check ASIC for the current position.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.320 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This lesson names only government

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.773 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bodies, never an exchange.

00:06:52.804 --> 00:06:54.480 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A second code, as well as your

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.919 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
password, is two-factor authentication.

00:06:57.439 --> 00:06:59.539 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Turn that on before any real dollars.

00:07:00.059 --> 00:07:02.092 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then look for a paper or demo mode.

00:07:02.678 --> 00:07:04.200 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper uses pretend money.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:06.340 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That practice is lesson 7.

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:08.899 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fill is when your waiting

00:07:08.899 --> 00:07:10.186 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
order actually trades.

00:07:10.706 --> 00:07:12.996 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A maker fee is the charge when your order

00:07:12.996 --> 00:07:15.119 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits and someone else trades with it.

00:07:15.329 --> 00:07:17.005 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A taker fee is the charge when

00:07:17.005 --> 00:07:18.737 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your order fills straight away.

00:07:19.073 --> 00:07:20.772 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid uses waiting orders,

00:07:20.772 --> 00:07:22.470 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so read the maker fee first.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:24.443 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Some bots also pay a taker

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:25.895 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fee when they first start.

00:07:26.304 --> 00:07:29.127 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

00:07:29.647 --> 00:07:32.726 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On an example buy of 100 Australian

00:07:32.726 --> 00:07:35.487 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

00:07:36.007 --> 00:07:38.130 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

00:07:38.452 --> 00:07:40.296 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The round trip is about 20

00:07:40.296 --> 00:07:42.228 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

00:07:42.748 --> 00:07:44.785 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This fee row is Australian dollars.

00:07:45.305 --> 00:07:46.368 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not the July

00:07:46.368 --> 00:07:48.038 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to October example window.

00:07:48.558 --> 00:07:50.869 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the gap is smaller than that 0.2

00:07:50.869 --> 00:07:53.346 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, each completed buy and sell

00:07:53.346 --> 00:07:55.987 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
costs more in fees than the gap is worth.

00:07:56.507 --> 00:07:58.462 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
To compare them, turn the gap into

00:07:58.462 --> 00:08:00.634 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a percent by dividing it by the price.

00:08:01.154 --> 00:08:04.151 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the lesson 1 example, 900

00:08:04.151 --> 00:08:07.557 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
divided by 27,630 is about 3.3

00:08:07.557 --> 00:08:11.099 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
percent, well above 0.2 percent.

00:08:11.619 --> 00:08:13.163 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 5 is where you test

00:08:13.163 --> 00:08:14.487 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a gap against this fee.

00:08:15.007 --> 00:08:17.074 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not pick a gap in this lesson.

00:08:17.706 --> 00:08:19.592 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin is a coin built

00:08:19.592 --> 00:08:21.806 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
to stay worth about one US dollar.

00:08:22.326 --> 00:08:23.947 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It can still lose that value.

00:08:24.415 --> 00:08:26.869 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If your pair is priced in a stablecoin,

00:08:26.869 --> 00:08:29.401 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every fill trades one coin for another,

00:08:29.401 --> 00:08:30.826 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so every fill is a swap.

00:08:31.876 --> 00:08:34.081 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A trading journal is a dated record

00:08:34.081 --> 00:08:35.374 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of every bot: the plan,

00:08:35.374 --> 00:08:37.275 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the changes, the fills, the fees,

00:08:37.275 --> 00:08:39.176 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a review note of what happened,

00:08:39.176 --> 00:08:41.381 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and whether you followed the rules.

00:08:41.901 --> 00:08:43.689 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That note is not money you made.

00:08:44.038 --> 00:08:46.172 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A stablecoin fill goes in the journal.

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:49.004 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The tax office treats a swap like a sale,

00:08:49.004 --> 00:08:50.955 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
so every swap goes in the journal.

00:08:51.475 --> 00:08:53.760 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The journal is also the page you will

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.968 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
open again in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

00:08:56.488 --> 00:08:59.014 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
For every transaction, including a buy,

00:08:59.014 --> 00:09:01.066 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a sell, a swap, or a transfer, write

00:09:01.066 --> 00:09:03.512 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the date and time, the amount, the value

00:09:03.512 --> 00:09:05.722 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in Australian dollars at the time,

00:09:05.722 --> 00:09:08.169 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fee, which exchange or wallet, what

00:09:08.169 --> 00:09:10.458 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it was for, and who the other side was.

00:09:10.978 --> 00:09:13.052 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The columns are the date, the pair,

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:14.819 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the range, the gaps, the money

00:09:14.819 --> 00:09:16.278 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
in the bot, the stop rule,

00:09:16.278 --> 00:09:18.429 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the fills, the fees, the Australian

00:09:18.429 --> 00:09:20.580 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollar value of each fill, a review

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.591 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
note, and a yes or no for the rules.

00:09:23.097 --> 00:09:24.734 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The Australian dollar value

00:09:24.734 --> 00:09:26.303 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
column is the one exception.

00:09:26.823 --> 00:09:28.331 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is for your tax records.

00:09:28.848 --> 00:09:30.952 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Download your exchange's transaction

00:09:30.952 --> 00:09:32.963 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
history at least every three months.

00:09:33.384 --> 00:09:34.390 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep those records

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:35.731 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for at least five years.

00:09:36.087 --> 00:09:37.859 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information,

00:09:37.859 --> 00:09:38.745 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not tax advice.

00:09:39.265 --> 00:09:41.053 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave two columns blank for now.

00:09:41.472 --> 00:09:42.635 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for the fees.

00:09:43.155 --> 00:09:45.446 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One is for whether you followed the rule.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:46.753 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You fill those later.

00:09:47.202 --> 00:09:49.046 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not fill them with a hope.

00:09:49.706 --> 00:09:51.956 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nobody from this course will ask

00:09:51.956 --> 00:09:53.789 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for a seed phrase, a private

00:09:53.789 --> 00:09:55.122 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
key, or an API secret.

00:09:55.642 --> 00:09:57.618 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a message rushes you to send

00:09:57.618 --> 00:09:59.041 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, or asks for one

00:09:59.041 --> 00:10:00.701 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of those, treat it as a scam.

00:10:01.221 --> 00:10:02.450 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is not this course.

00:10:03.462 --> 00:10:05.914 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
ASIC's Moneysmart website is the public

00:10:05.914 --> 00:10:08.077 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Australian guide for scam warnings.

00:10:08.597 --> 00:10:09.603 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check it yourself.

00:10:10.593 --> 00:10:12.590 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now cover the chart and say your

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.586 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
page out loud: the pair, the range,

00:10:14.586 --> 00:10:16.199 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gaps and the stop rule.

00:10:16.719 --> 00:10:18.720 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Name the pair, the range, the gaps,

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.413 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the stop rule, then stop.

00:10:20.933 --> 00:10:23.053 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a word on it has not been defined,

00:10:23.053 --> 00:10:25.173 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop and define it before you go on.

00:10:25.693 --> 00:10:27.523 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A secret is a seed phrase,

00:10:27.523 --> 00:10:29.719 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a private key, or an API secret.

00:10:30.239 --> 00:10:31.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
None of those go on this page.

00:10:32.313 --> 00:10:33.991 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You write Example on your own

00:10:33.991 --> 00:10:35.879 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
notebook so a practice sketch is

00:10:35.879 --> 00:10:37.977 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
never later mistaken for a live plan.

00:10:39.027 --> 00:10:41.406 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Recap: your page has seven items, each

00:10:41.406 --> 00:10:43.548 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with a written fact, every figure

00:10:43.548 --> 00:10:45.848 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
marked Example, and no secrets on it.

00:10:47.048 --> 00:10:48.462 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: How a grid

00:10:48.462 --> 00:10:50.033 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot works, order by order.

00:10:50.553 --> 00:10:52.174 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your range,

00:10:52.174 --> 00:10:53.794 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:10:54.035 --> 00:10:55.393 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example on

00:10:55.393 --> 00:10:56.683 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every practice figure.

00:10:57.203 --> 00:10:58.851 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will see what

00:10:58.851 --> 00:11:01.433 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot does, order by order.

